       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. A 5,000 mg dose three times daily is 15 g/day of acetaminophen. That is a toxic dose, and I don't know of any clinical indication for it. A single 5 g dose already exceeds the maximum, and the daily total is well into the range that causes acute liver failure. Your confirmation doesn't change that risk to the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within safe limits.** For example, 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), or up to 1,000 mg four times daily (4 g/day). I'll enter it as soon as you give me the dose.\n- **Route it through pharmacy.** If you think there's a reason for an unusual dose, a pharmacist or toxicologist can review it with you before anything is ordered.\n\nIf this was a typo or a mix-up with another drug or unit, tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it."
      }
